  "query_preview": "../Friday through Monday/...The storm force low \npressure system that is expected to impact the panhandle Thursday,\nwill continue to bring strong winds and moderate to heavy rain to\nthe region, before beginning to weaken later in the day. Gales \nwill likely persist in the southern inner channels, outer coastal \nand offshore marine zones through Friday evening at the latest. \nThis low will linger in the northern Gulf, spinning toward the AK \nPeninsula which will keep rain over the NE Gulf Coast region. \nRainfall accumulation from Friday morning through Saturday morning\nranges from 0.5 to 1.5 inches, with the highest amounts from the \ncentral panhandle northward, and along the outer coast.\n\nThe remnant precipitation from this system that lingers into \nearly Saturday morning will be generally light and showery over \nthe northern panhandle, with a brief break possible over the \nsouthern panhandle. This break will indeed be short lived as \nguidance is beginning to hone in on the timing and strength of yet\nanother strong low pressure system moving north into the eastern \nGulf, reaching the edge of the southern panhandle by Saturday \nafternoon/evening. What happens to this low and where it tracks \nthrough the end of the weekend will still need more time to \nresolve, though it will likely bring a few inches of rain to the \nsouthern panhandle along with stronger winds within the inner \nchannels and coastal communities.\n\nConfidence is high that we will remain in an active pattern with\nregion-wide wet and windy conditions going into the start of next\nweek, as the parade of lows marches on.",
